      {
        "id": 195357,
        "name": "NinjaMonkey",
        "username": "NinjaMonkey",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/67e7ee/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-04-11T15:48:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I understand the legal issues. And I agree, to an extent, that community made expansions don’t belong in official channels.</p>\n<p>I love SotM. I own the first edition, Enhanced Edition and every expansion including Villains which I never play. My biggest issue with it is the fiddliness  involved with the tabletop version. This issue makes the Villain style games unplayable for my group.</p>\n<p>Normally I play the game with friends or play on the app. This weekend I decided to break out the cards and go solo. 3 hours later after playing a single game and losing I questioned my life choices.</p>\n<p>I guess my point is that while I’m really coming around to the Cauldron, it’s not something I’ll ever really get a chance to play, which is a shame. For me, I would love to have these decks in an application mainly for the book-keeping so that I could actually play them.</p>\n<p>If Handelabra does eventually add a Steam Workshop option that would be great.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:22:40.323Z",
