        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/67e7ee/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-04-11T17:13:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>What was your setup that took 3 hours for a loss? Vengence format? That’s rough going for a solitare day.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I’ve had similar experiences before which is why I rarely break out the boxed set unless playing with friends. The time before this I was playing with the Dark Watch team but can’t remember the villain or the environment.</p>\n<p>This time around I was playing around with the Cauldron decks. Using Baccarat, Starlight, Malichae, and Necro versus Dendron in St. Simeon’s Catacombs.  It didn’t take long to get a feel for the heroes, villain, or environment.  Most of my time was spent tracking hit points, damage reduction, damage bonuses,  immunities, etc.</p>",
